CORE
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ reference member bound to x: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ moved: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The member was initialized by assigning the aggregate value through the
class's (deleted) operator=, which left the reference member unbound.
g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
